nt is covered**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n\\text{Point }(a,b) & \\text{on }L_{1}\\;(x=1) & \\text{on }L_{2}\\;(y=1) & \\text{on }L_{3}\\;(y=x)\\\\ \\hline\n(1,1) & \\checkmark & \\checkmark & \\checkmark\\\\\n(1,2) & \\checkmark &  &  \\\\\n(2,1) &  & \\checkmark &  \\\\\n(1,3) & \\checkmark &  &  \\\\\n(3,1) &  & \\checkmark &  \\\\\n(2,2) &  &  & \\checkmark\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThus each point of \\(\\mathcal{P}\\) lies on at least one of the three lines.\n\n**Count of sunny lines**\n\nAmong \\(\\{L_{1},L_{2},L_{3}\\}\\) only \\(L_{3}\\) is sunny, so the configuration contains exactly \\(k=1\\) sunny line.\n\nHence for \\(n=3\\) a configuration with exactly one sunny line exists. \u220e"
